(obligation (id "OB-GC-ENV-TRANSLATION-INPUTS") (contract_id "rv64gc-lab-env-v1") (contract_version "1") (profile_ids "rv64gc-lab-v0") (direction environment-assumption) (statement "The environment answers every page-table walk read - the WalkAccess request, an 8-byte PHYSICAL read of one PTE, a kind of its own and never a data Load - from the same main memory the hart's stores write, so a walk sees the latest entry the hart stored; no translation input exists besides that memory and the hart's own satp and TLB. The environment never writes a PTE (Svade: an A/D update the walk needs is the hart's page fault). A walk read the environment refuses is reported as the ORIGINAL access's access fault (1, 5 or 7), never a page fault. False if a walk read returned anything but the stored bytes, or the environment wrote a PTE.") (authority laboratory) (source_refs (source_id "RVP-SUPERVISOR") (locator "§11.1.3.2")) (source_refs (source_id "RVP-SUPERVISOR") (locator "§11.1.3.1")) (parameters (param (name walk_request_kind) (value (str "WalkAccess"))) (param (name environment_writes_ptes) (value (false)))) (required_checks "CHK-GC-ENV-TRANSLATION-INPUTS-POS") (required_checks "CHK-GC-ENV-TRANSLATION-INPUTS-NEG"))
(obligation (id "OB-GC-ENV-INTERRUPT-SOURCES") (contract_id "rv64gc-lab-env-v1") (contract_version "1") (profile_ids "rv64gc-lab-v0") (direction environment-assumption) (statement "Version 1's environment supplies NO interrupt source: the M-level pending bits MSIP, MTIP and MEIP read as 0 and a software write cannot set them (the laboratory platform declares no CLINT and no PLIC - a platform that supplies them is a later contract version, P5-BOARD's); STIP is the hart's own comparison of time against stimecmp (Sstc); SSIP and SEIP are set and cleared only by software. False if any pending bit became 1 without the hart's own comparison or a software write of a software-writable bit.") (authority laboratory) (source_refs (source_id "RVP-MACHINE") (locator "§2.1.1.9")) (source_refs (source_id "RVP-SSTC") (locator "12.1")) (parameters (param (name supplied_interrupt_sources) (value (int 0))) (param (name stip_source) (value (str "the hart: time >= stimecmp")))) (required_checks "CHK-GC-ENV-INTERRUPT-SOURCES-POS") (required_checks "CHK-GC-ENV-INTERRUPT-SOURCES-NEG"))
(obligation (id "OB-GC-ENV-VIRTUAL-TIME") (contract_id "rv64gc-lab-env-v1") (contract_version "1") (profile_ids "rv64gc-lab-v0") (direction environment-assumption) (statement "The environment's time supply IS the hart's virtual-time domain: time and mcycle advance by exactly one at every step boundary - a step that retired an instruction, one that delivered a trap, and one that found the hart waiting alike - while instret advances only on retirement; a waiting hart's time keeps advancing, so a timer wake reaches it WITHOUT retirement. No wall clock and no host time reaches the guest. False if time stood still while the hart waited, moved with host time, or instret counted a trap or a halted step.") (authority laboratory) (source_refs (source_id "RVI-ZICNTR") (locator "6.1")) (source_refs (source_id "RVP-MACHINE") (locator "§2.1.3.3")) (parameters (param (name ticks_per_step_boundary) (value (int 1))) (param (name host_time_visible) (value (false)))) (required_checks "CHK-GC-ENV-VIRTUAL-TIME-POS") (required_checks "CHK-GC-ENV-VIRTUAL-TIME-NEG"))
(obligation (id "OB-GC-ENV-RESERVATION-EVENTS") (contract_id "rv64gc-lab-env-v1") (contract_version "1") (profile_ids "rv64gc-lab-v0") (direction environment-assumption) (statement "Version 1's environment delivers NO reservation-invalidation event: one hart and no other agent writing memory, so a reservation's lifetime is entirely the hart's own rules (an LR replaces it, any SC clears it, a trap does not - OB-RESERVATION), and the eventuality the A chapter requires of a constrained LR/SC loop holds trivially: its first SC succeeds. A multi-agent environment is a later contract version (MC-MULTICORE). False if a reservation vanished without an LR or SC of the hart's own, or a constrained loop's first SC failed.") (authority laboratory) (source_refs (source_id "RVI-A") (locator "12.1.2")) (source_refs (source_id "RVI-RVWMO") (locator "17.1")) (parameters (param (name invalidation_events) (value (int 0))) (param (name constrained_loop_first_sc_succeeds) (value (true)))) (required_checks "CHK-GC-ENV-RESERVATION-EVENTS-POS") (required_checks "CHK-GC-ENV-RESERVATION-EVENTS-NEG"))
(obligation (id "OB-GC-PRIV-INSNS-V1") (contract_id "rv64gc-lab-env-v1") (contract_version "1") (profile_ids "rv64gc-lab-v0") (direction cpu-guarantee) (statement "The privileged system instructions behave per mode: mret/sret execute in their mode or higher and raise illegal-instruction below it (sret also raises in S when mstatus.TSR=1); a legal wfi ENTERS the wait - it retires, then the hart stalls and issues no fetch until a locally-enabled pending interrupt (at any privilege level, regardless of the global enables and of mideleg) wakes it, the no-op latitude recorded but not taken (P4-SYSTEM.5); wfi raises illegal-instruction in U (S is present) and in S when mstatus.TW=1; sfence.vma raises illegal-instruction in U and in S with mstatus.TVM=1, and invalidates the modelled TLB by the specification's four rs1/rs2 cases (P4-SYSTEM.3). xRET pops the two-level privilege stack (xIE<-xPIE, mode<-xPP, xPIE<-1, xPP<-U), clears MPRV when the target is not M, and sets pc<-xepc. Supersedes v0's OB-GC-PRIV-INSNS, which described wfi and sfence.vma as no-ops before the wait state and the TLB existed.") (authority architecture) (source_refs (source_id "RVP-INSNS") (locator "18.1")) (source_refs (source_id "RVP-MACHINE") (locator "2.1.3.2")) (source_refs (source_id "RVP-MACHINE") (locator "2.1.3.3")) (source_refs (source_id "RVP-SUPERVISOR") (locator "11.1.2.1")) (parameters (param (name supersedes) (value (str "OB-GC-PRIV-INSNS")))) (required_checks "CHK-GC-PRIV-INSNS-V1-POS") (required_checks "CHK-GC-PRIV-INSNS-V1-NEG"))
(obligation (id "OB-GC-ECALL-EBREAK-V1") (contract_id "rv64gc-lab-env-v1") (contract_version "1") (profile_ids "rv64gc-lab-v0") (direction cpu-guarantee) (statement "ECALL and EBREAK raise synchronous exceptions the architecture DELIVERS: ecall's cause names the originating mode (8 from U, 9 from S, 11 from M) with xtval 0, ebreak's is 3 with xtval the instruction's own address; delegation (medeleg) chooses the M or S handler, xepc is the instruction's own address, and execution continues in the handler - never a report to the harness. Supersedes the mirrored v0 OB-ECALL-EBREAK, whose rv64i wording (no privileged modes, a harness report, execution stops) is the base profile's, not this one's.") (authority architecture) (source_refs (source_id "RVP-MACHINE") (locator "2.1.3.1")) (source_refs (source_id "RVP-MACHINE") (locator "2.1.1.8")) (parameters (param (name supersedes) (value (str "OB-ECALL-EBREAK")))) (required_checks "CHK-GC-ECALL-EBREAK-V1-POS") (required_checks "CHK-GC-ECALL-EBREAK-V1-NEG"))
